Build a web magazine based on the attached PRD. Important: All UI elements, labels, and menus must be in Korean as specified, but follow the English technical instructions for the structure and features.

🎭 [PRD] Single-Author Theater Web Magazine: 구경꾼 (The Spectator)
1. Project Core Identity
Service Name: 구경꾼 (Display this in Korean)

Slogan: 연극을 보고, 듣고, 기록하기 (Display this in Korean)

Mission: A professional web magazine providing deep-dive reviews, industry news, and play curations for theater enthusiasts.

Language Requirement: The entire User Interface (UI), menus, buttons, and labels must be in Korean.

2. Visual & UI/UX Requirements (English Instructions)
Concept: A hybrid of "Classic Magazine" and "Modern Minimalist."

Color Palette: Clean white background (#FFFFFF) with high-contrast black text (#000000).

Typography: Use a sophisticated Serif font for main articles to give a "printed magazine" feel, and a clean Sans-serif for navigation.

Header Layout:

Center-aligned logo "구경꾼" at the top.

Navigation menu below the logo with 4 categories: 리뷰(Review), 뉴스(News), 피처(Feature), 큐레이션(Curation).

Home Screen:

Show a grid-style preview of the 2-3 most recent articles for each category.

Include a simple search bar at the top right for title-based searches (Label: "검색").

3. Section Specifics (UI Labels in Korean)
3.1 리뷰 (Review)
List View: Each item must show a Thumbnail, Title, Star Rating (별점), and 3 Keyword Tags (키워드).

Article View: Must include a dedicated "Performance Info" (공연 정보) box containing: Title, Venue, and Period.

3.2 뉴스 (News)
List-style layout for domestic and international theater industry news.

3.3 피처 (Feature)
Typography-focused layout for long-form essays, critiques, and editorials.

3.4 큐레이션 (Curation)
Focused on introducing overseas plays. Must include a "Book Info" (도서 정보) section for Author and Original Title.

4. Admin & CMS Requirements (English Instructions)
Hybrid Writing Form: Create a custom editor for the admin.

Fixed Meta-fields (Input fields):

Star Rating (1-5 stars) for Reviews.

Tag inputs (max 3) for Keywords.

Structured fields for "Performance Info" and "Book Info."

Flexible Body Editor: A Rich Text Editor that supports:

Free text formatting and alignment.

Image and Video (YouTube/Vimeo) embedding.

Customizable font sizes for subheaders.

5. Technical Instructions for AI
Responsive Design: Ensure the magazine is mobile-friendly with a focus on readability.

Search Logic: Implement a simple client-side or server-side search that matches the "Title" of the articles.

Navigation: All category links must filter and display the respective content types correctly.
